<title>CANADA: Toronto stocks drop as Wall Street tumbles.</title>
<headline>Toronto stocks drop as Wall Street tumbles.</headline>
<text>
<p>CHANGE				    CHANGE</p>
<p>TSE	  6091.90    -53.60   HI 6159.18	    LO  6191.70</p>
<p>DJI	  6753.44    -80.04   GOLD (LONDON)   US$343.40 -2.30</p>
<p>FTSE100    4281.50    +20.60   GOLD (NY-COMEX) US$345.20 -1.20</p>
<p>NIKKEI    18185.97   -128.36   LME CASH NICKEL US$7485    +0.0</p>
<p>CANDLR	1.3445		 LME CASH ALUM   US$1594.0  -1.0</p>
<p>CAN 30-YR   111.05     +0.62   FEB BRENT CRUDE US$22.46  +0.04</p>
<p>--------------------MARKET COMMENT---------------------------- * Toronto stocks fell nearly one percent, following New York lower after it dropped on profit-taking in the high tech sector. * 120 million shares traded worth C$1.9 billion.</p>
<p>((Reuters Toronto Bureau (416) 941-8109))</p>
